<!--
  A paper lantern, cut as a seal.

  居場所 is both "whereabouts" and "the place where one belongs", and a lantern is
  what those two meanings have in common: a light left on so somebody can find
  their way back. It is not a pin on a map, because this app does not have a map
  and does not want one.

  Carved rather than drawn: the block is solid and the lantern is knocked out of
  it in white, the way a seal carries its design. That inverts the rest of the
  house, whose marks are black on white, and that is deliberate — a light only
  reads as a light if there is something dark around it.

  Two ribs, not three. Three was drawn first and at launcher size the white
  bands fell close to a pixel and the whole lantern started to go grey — the
  same failure that made the music box comb drop from eight teeth to four. Two
  at nearly twice the width keep the black-and-white alternation that makes a
  lantern read as a lantern.

  The block is sized so its corners survive a circular launcher mask, which is
  the harshest one in common use; a seal that gets masked into a disc is no
  longer a seal.
-->
